      "title": "Employee Directory - Real Northwind Employee Photos",
      "description": "Photos are stored as objects in the MinIO data lake (object storage), keyed by EmployeeCode -- the ClickHouse warehouse holds only the EmployeeCode -> PhotoUrl metadata pointer, not the image bytes themselves. This is the lakehouse pattern: bulky unstructured assets live in cheap object storage, while the warehouse stays lean and query-fast.",
